From 8c921325772713852cc1893d4a978fbff00f6269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:39:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] App device key for the Android app's background upload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Android app (now aMuseD1985/ElTouro-Android) uploads a running
recording with its own device key, so it keeps working when Android killed
the app and the WebView's cookies are gone.

- app_devices: SHA-256 of the key only, app version, created/last seen/
  revoked; FK ON DELETE CASCADE; at most five keys per rider
- app_device_lib.php, POST /api/app/device: register (session + X-CSRF),
  check and revoke (with the key)
- track.php: accepts Authorization: Bearer eld_… or X-Device-Token instead
  of session + CSRF – without tester cookie and session file, consent is
  checked; the cookie path is unchanged
- keys are revoked on logout and on password reset (which now also revokes
  the app's remember tokens)
- data export lists app_devices
- privacy policy DE+EN: new section "Android-App" with marker and the
  earlier default hashes; CONSENT_VERSION deliberately unchanged
- docs/app-interface.md: the contract between app and web app (copy of the
  file in the Android repo)
